# class Base { constructor(first, second) { first(); } }  class Derived extends Base { }  new Derived(one, two)
# The constructor that the language gives Derived is `constructor(...args) { super(...args) }`. It does nothing with the array of its rest parameter but spread it into one call, so nobody else
# gets hold of the array: it holds at each index what the caller has passed at that position, and each argument reaches the parameter of its position and no other.
